      "message": "Yeah, true. This usage of the NONE enum was a bit of a stretch, but removes some boiler plate.\n\nThe NONE name is more important to represent that there is actually no FAILED or PASSED status. I renamed it to DEFAULT to try to accommodate both use cases. If you still think this is not good enough, I can redesign this finish mechanism.",
